# N, THE INDUCTION INCIDENCE, PROJECTED TO WHAT A `categoryValueRef` CARRIES. One row per
# (filing, operation, layer): this operation induces into this layer, and the flow node says so
# itself rather than being collected by a container.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE DIRECTION IS THE WHOLE DIFFERENCE. A `lane` collects its members and a flow node can
#    be collected once. A `categoryValue` collects nobody: the MEMBER declares which categories it
#    is in, unbounded, so the cover may overlap and no container has to be enlarged to say so.
#    That is why this relation can be many-to-many where diagrams/lane_membership.sqlc cannot.
#
# ⭐⭐ MEASURED, AND EXERCISED RATHER THAN HYPOTHETICAL. In this corpus one operation both draws
#    from `labour` and induces into `capability`, so it belongs to two layers, and a lane set can
#    hold it in one. ⛔ With no relation for the cover, an emitter puts the operation in the
#    draw lane and the induction is absent from the artifact entirely.
#
# ⛔ INCIDENCE ONLY. The wider relation carries three points, a unit, a typed absence and
#   `decider`; none of it composes here, for the reason diagrams/lane_members.sqlc gives.
-- pm:Operation/pm:Induction as incidence; BPMN 2.0 tFlowElement/categoryValueRef.
SELECT i.filing, i.operation, i.layer
FROM (
    :compose(entries/inductions.sqlc)
) i
